<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buyeo Pung</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Prince Pung, Hōshō</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buyeo Pung was a prince of Baekje, son of its last king Uija, who lived at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamato-court">Yamato court</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> as a hostage. After Baekje fell to Tang and Silla in 660, the restoration leaders brought him back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> as king with Japanese support. When his forces and the Japanese fleet were defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-baekgang">Battle of Baekgang</a> in 663, he fled to Goguryeo; after its fall in 668 he was exiled by the Tang.</p></div>
